{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Asaf.</b> He brought her in to a place where she would not be seen — and so ״אֱסֹף חֶרְפָּתֵנוּ״ (Isaiah 4), ״וְלֹא יֵאָסֵף הַבַּיִתָה״ (Exodus 9), ״אָסְפוּ נָגְהָם״ (Joel 4), ״וִירֵחֵךְ לֹא יֵאָסֵף״ (Isaiah 60) — he would not be hidden away." "<b>My disgrace.</b> That I was a disgrace, for I was barren, and they would say about me that I would go up to the portion of Esau the wicked. And its aggadah: so long as a woman has no son, she has no one on whom to hang her sourness; once she has a son, she hangs it on him: Who broke this vessel? Your son. Who ate these figs? Your son."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:17.477550916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}